WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.689
I purchased a microscope near Qasr El Einy in Cairo.

00:00:04.689 --> 00:00:08.828
It was not laboratory equipment assigned to me by a university.

00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:18.980
Bringing it with me to Qatar was a considerable hassle.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:22.285
The difficulty did not end when I had paid for it.

00:00:27.967 --> 00:00:31.910
With a microscope at home, observation no longer depended

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.854
entirely on laboratory booking hours or a scheduled class.

00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:45.889
The instrument let me pursue small independent

00:00:45.889 --> 00:00:49.394
observations simply because I wanted to understand something.

00:00:55.258 --> 00:00:59.081
Ownership did not confer a scientific result; it

00:00:59.081 --> 00:01:02.903
made curiosity more practical by providing repeated access.

00:01:09.258 --> 00:01:13.467
Years later, across developmental biology and materials science, I still

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:17.676
recognise the value of being able to look for myself.
